{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Sign","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.coupling_vanishes_on_charge_bilinears","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.coupling_vanishes_on_charge_bilinears","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L248-L261","doc":"**The D2 obstruction, audit-shaped corollary.** An S₃-equivariant coupling\nfunctional LINEAR in the antisymmetric invariant μ̄(123) vanishes on every\ncharge bilinear: `∑ₖ T(μ̄)ₖ · qᵢqⱼ = 0` for all charges.  The EM coupling\nfunctional of the audit therefore cannot couple through μ̄ linearly — only\nthrough |μ̄| (see `muBarFamily_sq_invariant`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.equivariant_linearMap_eq_zero_of_neZero_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.equivariant_linearMap_eq_zero_of_neZero_two","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L232-L246","doc":"Convenience version: the 2-torsion-freeness hypothesis discharged from\n`[NoZeroDivisors R]` + `[NeZero (2 : R)]` (e.g. `R = ℤ`, `ℚ`, or any\nintegral domain of characteristic ≠ 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.equivariant_linearMap_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.equivariant_linearMap_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L205-L230","doc":"**Finding D2 (main theorem).** Any S₃-equivariant `R`-linear map from the\nsign representation (the line spanned by μ̄(123)) to the pair-channel\nrepresentation (charge bilinears; trivial ⊕ standard) is ZERO — the\nconcrete Schur-lemma obstruction, over any commutative ring without\n2-torsion (weakest hypothesis stated explicitly). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.sign_equivariant_pairVector_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.sign_equivariant_pairVector_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L181-L203","doc":"Core computation: a pair-channel vector `v` that transforms in the SIGN\nrepresentation — `sgn(g)·v k = v (g⁻¹ k)` for all `g` — vanishes,\nprovided `R` has no 2-torsion.  Proof: each channel `k` is fixed by the\ntransposition of the two other indices, which has sign −1, so\n`−v k = v k`.  This is the \"sign rep does not occur in trivial ⊕\nstandard\" Schur statement, by direct computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.chargeBilinear_equivariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.chargeBilinear_equivariant","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L170-L177","doc":"The pair-index bijection (pair ↔ omitted component) is S₃-EQUIVARIANT:\nthe charge bilinear intertwines the component action `q ↦ q ∘ g⁻¹` with\nthe pair-channel action `pairAct`.  This is the proved bridge between the\nphysical charge-bilinear space and the `Fin 3 → R` model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.prod_compl_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.prod_compl_map","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L159-L168","doc":"Reindexing a complement-product along a permutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.chargeBilinear_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.chargeBilinear_two","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L154-L157","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.chargeBilinear_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.chargeBilinear_one","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L149-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.chargeBilinear_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.chargeBilinear_zero","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L144-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.chargeBilinear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.chargeBilinear","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L137-L142","doc":"The charge bilinear of the pair channel `k`: the product `q_i q_j` over\nthe two components `{i,j} = {k}ᶜ` other than `k`.  For ³He-type charges\n`q = (1,1,0)` exactly one channel is EM-active; for ³H-type `q = (1,0,0)`\nevery channel vanishes (D1 of the audit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.pairAct_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.pairAct_mul","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L131-L135","doc":"`pairAct` is a left action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.pairAct_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.pairAct_one","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L128-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.pairAct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.pairAct","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L120-L125","doc":"The S₃ action on pair-channel functions.  Channels (unordered pairs\n`{i,j} ⊂ Fin 3`) are indexed by the omitted component `k`; the action of a\nrelabeling `g` sends the function `w` to `w ∘ g⁻¹`.  As a representation\nthis is the permutation module on 3 points = trivial ⊕ standard. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.muBarFamily_sq_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.muBarFamily_sq_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L109-L116","doc":"The quadratic invariant μ̄² is S₃-invariant: the sign-rep obstruction\nkills only the channel LINEAR in μ̄; a coupling through |μ̄|\n(equivalently μ̄²) survives, and is in particular mirror-insensitive —\nconsequence (i) of finding D2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.muBarFamily_swap_eq_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.muBarFamily_swap_eq_neg","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L101-L107","doc":"On an odd permutation (e.g. a mirror-inducing component transposition)\nthe invariant flips sign: the mirror link carries `μ̄ = −μ̄(123)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.muBarFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.muBarFamily","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L93-L99","doc":"The μ̄ family: the value of the antisymmetric invariant on the\n`g`-relabeled component ordering, `μ̄(g(1)g(2)g(3)) = sgn(g)·μ̄(123)`.\nThis transformation law is the probe-verified D2 input (integer Magnus,\n6/6 permutations exact; witness\n`computations/deltalambda/mirror-split-s3-em-functional.witness.json`) —\nit is the MODEL here, not a re-derivation of the Milnor invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.signR_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.signR_swap","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L84-L89","doc":"A transposition has sign −1 in `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.signR_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.signR_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L77-L82","doc":"Signs square to 1 in `R` (they are ±1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.signR_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.signR_mul","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L71-L75","doc":"`signR` is multiplicative — `g ↦ signR g * ·` really is a representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.signR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction.signR","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstruction.lean#L66-L69","doc":"The sign of a permutation of the three link components, cast into the\nbase ring `R`.  `g ↦ signR g * μ̄` is the sign representation of S₃ on the\none-dimensional space spanned by the antisymmetric invariant μ̄(123). ","signatureChunk":0}]}